@startuml
title Smart Campus Study Room Booking - Use-Case Diagram

left to right direction

actor Student
actor Administrator

rectangle "Smart Campus Study Room Booking System" {

    usecase "View Room\nAvailability" as UC_View
    usecase "Book Room" as UC_Book
    usecase "Cancel Own\nBooking" as UC_Cancel
    usecase "Receive\nConfirmation" as UC_Confirm

    usecase "Block / Unblock\nRoom" as UC_Block
    usecase "Review Room\nUsage" as UC_Usage
}

' Student goals
Student -- UC_View
Student -- UC_Book
Student -- UC_Cancel
Student -- UC_Confirm

' Administrator goals
Administrator -- UC_Block
Administrator -- UC_Usage

' Confirmation is a required result of successful booking/cancellation
UC_Book ..> UC_Confirm : <<include>>
UC_Cancel ..> UC_Confirm : <<include>>

note bottom of UC_View
Assumption:
Availability reflects existing
bookings and blocked rooms.
end note

note bottom of UC_Book
Assumptions / rules:
- Start time is in the future.
- Duration > 0 and <= 2 hours.
- Same-room active bookings
  cannot overlap.
- Touching bookings are allowed.
- A blocked room cannot accept
  a new booking.
- Exactly 2 hours is allowed.
end note

note bottom of UC_Cancel
Assumption:
The Student can cancel only
a booking that they made.
end note

note bottom of UC_Confirm
Assumption:
Confirmation is provided only
after a booking or cancellation
completes successfully.
end note

note bottom of UC_Block
Assumptions:
- Blocking prevents new bookings.
- Existing bookings are not
  automatically cancelled.
- Unblocking allows the room to
  become available again.
end note

note bottom of UC_Usage
Assumption:
Usage is based on booking
information over a selected period.
end note

legend bottom
  Rules:
  R1 - Future start; duration > 0 and <= 2 hours.
  R2 - Active bookings for the same room cannot overlap.
  R3 - A blocked room cannot accept a new booking.
  R4 - A successful booking produces a confirmation.

  Out of scope:
  payments, room equipment, recurring bookings,
  waiting lists, notifications other than confirmation,
  and user registration.

  <<include>> rationale:
  Receive Confirmation is included by Book Room and
  Cancel Own Booking because confirmation is a required
  outcome when either action completes successfully.

  No <<extend>> relationship is used because none of the
  approved stories describes optional behaviour that
  conditionally extends another use case.
endlegend

@enduml